// A module may hold the three collections as state — E013 used to allow only
// scalars, which is why four applications wrote their translation tables as
// `??` chains inside a function: it was the only way to put a table in a
// module.

<# ./module_collection_state_m => m

// Exported collection constants, read from outside.
>> m.LADOS ¶
>> m.TABLA ¶
>> m::lado(2) ¶

// Private dictionary state, read by key.
>> m::etiqueta("dos") ¶
>> m::etiqueta("tres") ¶

// A key added to module state stays added.
m::guardar("tres", "tercero")
>> m::etiqueta("tres") ¶
>> m::privado() ¶

// A dictionary nested inside a dictionary — the JSON shape.
>> m::anidado("en") ¶
>> m::anidado("es") ¶
